{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1107527-need-chiminage-ideas-for-raven","id":1107527,"title":"Need Chiminage Ideas for Raven","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-24T23:00:57-07:00","id":1107527,"title":"Need Chiminage Ideas for Raven","content":"A character intends to get a Raven spirit to help him. This isn't fetish level chiminage, but more like Rite of Binding for services or as talens. What would be appropriate chiminage to the spirit?<br /> <br /> Raven spirits are trickster based, so they typically enjoy some kind of display of ingenuity or trickery. Axis Mundi gives an example for Hrafn that to agree to become a fetish, the Garou needs to trick a Wyrm minion do Gaia's bidding or some other &quot;epic&quot; prank. Wow, that's really hard - but I understand that's appropriate for a fetish. For a talen or single service, it won't need to be at that level. To learn Gifts, the Garou would need to solve three riddles which is simply an Enigmas roll. Talen/Binding has to be somewhere inbetween.<br /> <br /> I need some ideas that the Garou could perform to get the raven spirit to comply. I know there are various kinds of deception, theft, rule breaking, or using one's wits to survive that would work. It's just making them relevant to raven.<br /> <br /> Any kind of help would be appreciated! And feel free to share any stories of chiminage to other spirits you've seen in your games. You never know what can help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T23:30:39-07:00","id":1107539,"title":"","content":"Hang some shiny stuff in a tree, a very tall tree. Then tell the raven spirit about it, but only what tree it is in if they agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:14:44-07:00","id":1107627,"title":"","content":"Secrets are an easy one. The player has to give Raven a secret. Depending on the severity of the Secret, how many people are involved, and who is involved; The more bargaining powers the character has with Raven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T08:47:20-07:00","id":1107647,"title":"","content":"The eye ball of a living and at the same time dead creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T09:56:21-07:00","id":1108437,"title":"","content":"A. The Garou must steal an item of need and gift it to Raven or a person, group or hero of Raven's choosing. For example. The wolf must hack into a lab's computers and pass any incriminating information on to an animal right's activist. The wolf must steal a fetish from a mage and pass it on to a raven kinfolk. <br /> <br /> B. The werewolf must play a trick upon an enemy of raven. Owl has made his nest in the traditional roosting grounds of crow and his fellows. The Garou must trick Owl into moving somewhere far away from Raven and his followers. <br /> <br /> C. Although typically the role of Owl, Raven is also loosely associated with death. Raven needs a wolf to escort a soul to the underworld. <br /> <br /> D. The werewolf must share his deepest secret. This could be with an enemy, the Sept, Raven or some other individual. <br /> <br /> E. Raven requires an Omen to be given but cannot do so himself, for reasons. The werewolf must act in Raven's behalf. <br /> <br /> F. Mortal Children have been harassing the local flock. The werewolves must scare the children into behaving. Or a group of masked men (University Students) have been kidnapping Raven's mortal children (or lesser spirits), performing social experiments upon them, tagging them and then releasing them. Crow wants the werewolf to put a stop to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T20:25:52-07:00","id":1108608,"title":"","content":"Thanks for everyone's contributions. Some of these have given me ideas to think about. Coming up with appropriate chiminage ideas that can scale and be modified is something I always like as I need them! I would have liked to see more of that in the Player's or Storyteller's Guides.<br /> <br /> If anyone else would like to contribute, please continue to do so!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T15:17:30-07:00","id":1108972,"title":"","content":"Caring for Raven's living children could be a simple form of chiminage. Leave out interesting and shiny objects and bits of food for ravens to find, potentially helping to protect a nesting site from predators or humans for a breeding season is another. I had a raven spirit in a Wild West game I ran accept chiminage in the form of hand made shiny wind chimes with riddles inscribed on the chimes hung on several trees in a forest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}